# J2 GUI run editors implementation checkpoint

Workspace `effective-config/G4UniversalSim`, branch `roadmap/J2-F8-editing`, baseline `fc606739b9bb5b381b87d5ffd2870844c10afee2`. No commit, no global build. Shared pre-existing/other-agent changes untouched. Status: own implementation frozen and handed off; final own smoke 223 v3 entrances, two legacy smokes passed; independent reviewer Sagan `01a197d6-adc1-75b0-bb56-7123f75bab20` rechecked and closed all three findings. No native/Geant4 acceptance claim. Final review receipt: `out/collab/j2-run-editors/review.md`.

## Ownership and API

- Existing `SourceEditableModel`: new `gps_sources: list[GPSDefinition]`, `multiple_vertex: bool`, `phase_space_file: str`, `phase_space_recycle: bool`. Empty sources+empty replay retains exact legacy/default source behavior. Named sources replace legacy fields only in writer; inactive legacy values remain saved. Replay and named sources conflict and block generation, never silently choose one.
- Existing `PhysicsEditableModel`: new `replace_modules: list[str]`, `regions: list[RegionDefinition]`, `fields: list[FieldDefinition]`, `bias_rules: list[BiasRuleDefinition]`. Reuse existing `mode/reference_list/default_cut/enable_biasing_physics/extra_modules/manual_modules/particle_cuts`.
- `core/run_editor_model.py`: row dataclasses, supported enums/constructor allowlist, pure validators, `source_values`, `region_values`, `physics_sections`, `hydrate_extensions`. No resource IO, subprocess or transaction owner. Strings deliberately retain illegal drafts. Writer only emits active distribution parameters.
- `widgets/config/j2_run_editors.py`: `J2RunEditors.set_models(source,physics)` / `collect_into(source,physics)` / `changed`; `row_editors[key]` supplies `rows`, `controls`, `labels`, `list`, `set_rows`. Source/region/field/bias list + details; constructor selectors use add/remove list. Projections/selections do not emit changes.
- Existing `RunConfigMixin._populate_sps_editors()` projects advanced rows; `_update_j2_run_editors()` collects into original owners, validates and calls original `_emit_changed()`. Existing `_adopt` exposes `j2_run_editors` to ConfigBuilderPage automatically. No config_builder_page edits.
- `project.py` hydrates nested new row objects after existing strict dataclass validation. Per main-agent decision, SCHEMA_VERSION is now 8 (ordinary legacy 1–7 continue known defaults); no document creation changes. `asdict` naturally includes all drafts in ordinary JSON/F5 snapshots. Main agent owns explicit old-v7 complete-snapshot migration in edit_snapshot.py; never generically fill arbitrary missing fields in a new complete v8 snapshot.

### Exact added fields for v7 snapshot migration

`SourceEditableModel`: `gps_sources=[]`, `multiple_vertex=false`, `phase_space_file=""`, `phase_space_recycle=false`.

`PhysicsEditableModel`: `replace_modules=[]`, `regions=[]`, `fields=[]`, `bias_rules=[]`.

There are no other new top-level project or existing source/physics dataclass fields. Nested GPSDefinition is entirely new: `editor_id` (UUID hex; default generated once per new row/old explicitly supported import), name/intensity/particle/ion_z/ion_a/ion_charge/ion_excitation/energy_type/energy/energy_sigma/energy_min/energy_max/alpha/ezero/spectrum_file/position_type/shape/center/radius/inner_radius/halfx/halfy/halfz/beam_sigma/beam_sigma_x/beam_sigma_y/rot1/rot2/confine/angular/direction/min_theta/max_theta/angular_sigma/angular_sigma_x/angular_sigma_y/focus. Other nested classes' exact fields/defaults are in core/run_editor_model.py, all new under the new empty lists (not old-v7 mandatory fields).

Source editor_id is separate from editable section name and list index. Rename and move preserve ID, duplicate assigns a fresh ID/name, save/open and F5 replay preserve IDs/order. INI emits names and textual row order but never editor_id; no claim that backend enumeration/native source indices follow GUI row order. Structure actions also have `.move_up/.move_down` object names. Selection restoration prefers stable ID.

