## Main-agent integration patches required (not applied here)

F4 adapter API added: `validate_gps(row, "source.gps_sources[N]", issues=issues)` and `validate_physics_extensions(model, issues=issues)` append `(machine_path, reason_i18n_key)` tuples alongside their unchanged list-of-display-errors return. Paths are generated by producer rules, not reverse-parsed translated prose. The main diagnostic adapter can use path→editor/collection/row/field and GPS row `editor_id` as entity, with FIELD_LABELS for display; duplicate source names/IDs and source mode conflicts remain explicit source-model validator rules.

1. `window/transactions.py`: F5 current/undo/restore already traverses sourceEditor/physicsEditor JSON, but dynamic controls/structure actions must enter the original transaction notification path. Stable object names: `j2.source.multiple_vertex`, `j2.source.phase_space_file`, `j2.source.phase_space_recycle`; row controls `j2.{gps_sources|regions|fields|bias_rules}.{dataclass_field}`; row actions `.add/.duplicate/.remove`; module controls `j2.{extra_modules|replace_modules|manual_modules}.{list|choice|add|remove}`; cuts `j2.cuts.{gamma|e-|e+|proton}`. Raw values live in dataclass strings; avoid projecting stale selected-row drafts over a new selection or undo model. Row selection itself is view state. Recommended register objectName tokens, resolve through `j2_run_editors.row_editors[key].controls`, reproject from the restored model.
2. `core/edit_state.py`/view projection whitelist: permit the above stable bindings if captured; no protocol expansion necessary. Include module structures and row collections in transaction boundary labels/merge keys. New controls must use existing Ctrl+Z ownership, not QLineEdit local undo.
3. `config_validator.py`: validate new models and remove old unconditional generated-bias hook blockade only after rule validation. Require enabled process rules and hook together. Structured fields do not bypass backend validation; actual particle/process/region/field-map/spectrum validation remains necessary. Do not infer observed/applied or physical correctness from GUI acceptance.
4. `package_writer.py`: copy/rebase spectrum files, phase-space input lists and electric/magnetic maps through existing package source provenance service (no new file owner); update cloned model paths before main writer, preserve user model paths and hashes. New external dependencies cannot remain machine-relative after exporting/moving a package.
5. Preview: if `sourceEditor.gps_sources` or `.phase_space_file` is nonempty, suppress legacy source rays and label advanced source preview unavailable. Do not render stale legacy source as the actual named/replay source. Existing geometry truth remains unchanged. Summary widgets should show named/replay mode, not imply legacy energy/position edits affect the active source.
6. Translation: new JSON to be supplied beside this report; import into central i18n once. New text uses `ui_text` keys. DeepSeek advice accepted: list+detail, experimental labels and planned-vs-observed distinction; no raw INI editor or new runtime observation owner.

## Old run-package restoration (project_snapshot.py)

Current adapter restores snapshot-recorded source/physics, not CURRENT main.ini. New ordinary JSON hydration alone cannot make missing historical advanced fields safe. Required policy: read/hash CURRENT main.ini via existing package input reader, parse supported source/physics/field/bias sections, reconstruct typed rows (including process case), or explicitly reject an unsupported/unrepresentable current section. Never fall back to legacy/default single source while a named/phase-space section exists. Preserve current material/geometry reconstruction and old success invalidation. Snapshot JSON containing new rows hydrates, but it is historical evidence and cannot substitute current package text.

Suggested mapping: `[source]/multiple_vertex`; all `[source.name]` to `GPSDefinition` (`position` or `center`→center; `angular=isotropic`+theta keys→GUI cone; ion tokens→ion_z/a/charge/excitation; distribution-inactive drafts default only when absent); `[source]/phase_space_file/recycle` mutually exclusive with named GPS; manual `[physics] reference=` + modules includes EM; extra/replace vectors; `[physics.cuts]`; `[physics.region.Name]` with e-/e+→electron/positron; `[field]` empty name vs `[field.Name]` volumes; `[biasing.xs.particle.Process]` preserve process original case. If unsupported aliases/module capabilities/phase-space output or unknown fields cannot be represented, report blocker and keep captured source evidence, never silently discard them. Backend-observed EffectiveConfig and historical results remain separate.

