## Follow-up scope accepted 2026-11-02 (CURRENT import / preview / interaction)

Main now owns source_physics_scoring_model.py validation, transactions.py, config_validator.py, diagnostic_navigation.py and central i18n.py. This follow-up does not edit them. Existing import adapter located in core/project_snapshot.py; existing source draw owner is preview3d/source_builder.py, used by both scene_builder and backend geometry overlay.

### F5 widget API (implemented)

- `J2RunEditors.interaction_controls()` / alias `editable_controls()` → `dict[str,QWidget]`. Includes mutable row details, row lists/actions, constructor choices/lists/actions, replay/simultaneous controls and cuts. Immutable `GPS.editor_id` is excluded. All bindings satisfy edit_state machine grammar. Cuts use `j2.cuts.electron` / `.positron`; collections use `j2.gps_sources.*`, `.regions.*`, `.fields.*`, `.bias_rules.*`. Source shape tokens remain interface values, not translated labels.
- `collect_into(source,physics)` first captures all controls in each CURRENT selected row, including raw `setText` that emitted no textEdited. Unselected rows remain as stored. Full raw values live in existing model strings, including illegal/unfinished input. No extra draft map; no stale path draft can overwrite a relocated model. is_dirty is set only for a model owner whose relevant values actually changed (already dirty stays dirty).
- `selection_state()` → `dict[str,int]`: `j2.tabs`, `j2.{gps_sources|regions|fields|bias_rules|extra_modules|replace_modules|manual_modules}.selection`. `restore_selection()` validates keys/ranges first, accepts partial view hints, blocks all interaction signals, never emits changed. Restore after model projection. Row -1 denotes no selection. Source set_rows still prefers editor_id when preserving an existing selection across a reordered projection.

### CURRENT INI import (implemented)

- New `core/run_editor_import.py`: `parse_run_editor_ini(text, source_path=..., previous_source=...)` and `load_run_editor_ini(path, previous_source=...)`. Closed supported source/physics/field/process-bias mapping, named source IDs preserved by existing name; legacy single-source settings retain their legacy editor. Preset values are materialized from supported backend presets. Incomplete declared distributions are refused rather than filled with convenient GUI defaults. Comma vectors are decoded with backend per-component units, whitespace shared-unit vectors are decoded separately, then stored in canonical mm.
- Unknown key/section, unsupported main format and unrepresentable current fields raise `RunEditorImportError`. Exception contains `source_path`, exact `raw_text` including physical newline bytes decoded as UTF-8, SHA-256, and `ImportIssue(section,key,value,line,reason)` tuples. Import refuses publication, preserves the previous GUI project and the source file; it never returns a default model after dropping unknown content. Raw capture is source evidence, not proof of runtime application. Known invalid numeric drafts remain strings for normal editor validation.
- `core/project_snapshot.py` now reads CURRENT main.ini source/physics/field/bias. It still restores material/geometry from CURRENT actual package files and rejects contradictory declared standard paths. Resource references (multiple replay files, active spectra, field maps) are resolved and individually hashed/read inside the current package. Geometry file/copies_file imports still use the existing CURRENT geometry parser/adapter, so original snapshot geometryDocument/materialDocument drafts and old STL paths never replace materialized package inputs. Run/scoring remain snapshot-recorded; macro changes/old success/EffectiveConfig runtime evidence are not restored. This scope is explicit in returned notes.
- Existing snapshot-restore smoke intentionally modified CURRENT 7→99 MeV but expected 7. Its three outdated assertions now expect CURRENT 99; generated macro still uses snapshot-recorded 23 events, not edited 999, preserving the macro scope boundary.

### Source and Boolean preview / summaries (implemented)

- Advanced named/replay mode returns PreviewSource(generated=False, position=None, glyphs=[], rays=[], mode=unavailable) with a precise reason. No legacy particle/energy/position is rendered as current. Both editor scene and backend mesh overlay show the hidden-source reason.
- RunConfig status shows named count and simultaneous/intensity mode or replay, manual constructor count, reference add/replace counts. Legacy source tab/quick fields and inactive manual reference shortcuts are disabled with explanatory tooltip; original schema tooltips return in legacy mode. Bias checkbox no longer says external-input-only.
- Boolean tools forward shape_properties into preview parameter decoding and solid_mesh validation. Renderer already deliberately hides Boolean overlays; each tool now has an explicit not_drawn reason (or actual unsupported-shape/missing-property diagnostic), no guessed geometry. Target still shows its pre-CSG solid with the existing warning; backend geometry remains the CSG truth.

